[h1]Changelog[/h1]

[h2]4.1: Loose Ends[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Operative fates are now reported.[/b] You are told when one of your agents is captured (and by whom, when known), executed, or slips a counter-intelligence net and makes it home.
[*][b]Assassination victims notice.[/b] The target country now learns that a death was an assassination, or that a plot against its leader was foiled - the sponsor stays unnamed.
[*][b]Steal Technology[/b] now requires the target to lead you in technologies, and says so. Reaching parity mid-operation recalls the agent with a notification instead of ending silently.
[*][b]Director of Intelligence[/b] bonus is permanent while one is seated - no more monthly "modifier gained" spam or countdown.
[*][b]External Security laws[/b] are gated on later technologies (Central Archives, Identification Documents, Political Agitation) instead of all being available in 1836. Already-enacted laws are kept.
[*][b]AI election interference[/b] backs an opposition party rather than any party at random.
[*]Clandestine Arms Pipeline: the defiance payoff is judged when the pipeline winds down, and only if the recipient came through the war intact.
[*]Kompromat: a disgraced commander is always released after twelve months, even if the scheduled release is lost.
[*]Naval Intelligence Network has its own lens icon (it reused Sow Discontent's).
[*]Removed a diplomatic catalyst that could no longer fire.
[*]Save-compatible with 4.0.
[/list]

[h2]4.0: Operatives[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Espionage is now genuinely secret.[/b] Operations no longer create diplomatic pacts and no cost modifiers betray your budget: nothing appears in any diplomacy panel, spending is drawn straight from the treasury, and a target learns it is being worked on only when your people are caught.
[*][b]NEW: Operatives.[/b] Recruit named agents with tradecraft specialties - cryptographer, saboteur, master of disguise, silver tongue. Every operation asks who goes and cannot run without someone free; the right specialist tilts the odds. Time on assignment builds experience through Seasoned, Veteran and Master Spy: better odds, better escape chances, and unbreakable silence under interrogation at the top of the ladder.
[*][b]NEW: The Intelligence Console.[/b] A full command panel inside the Shadow War journal entry: your roster with portraits, live status and wages; a Director of Intelligence promoted from the ranks (fire one and their interest group seethes - and one in four sells everything to a hostile power); every running operation with its target's flag, its own monthly cost and its agent's portrait; the total agency budget; election ballots and the sealed train manifest.
[*][b]NEW: Spies on the government payroll.[/b] Wages scale with your economy, each agent's experience, and the government wage level you set. Pay Low and idle operatives risk defecting each year - twice as likely at Very Low. The buyer decides their fate: pay for the dossier and every operation against them is rolled up at once, pay extra to poach the agent onto their own roster, or turn the traitor away - and half the time the treachery is caught coming home.
[*][b]NEW: Counterespionage coups.[/b] Catch a foreign agent in the act and move on them, with odds set by the espionage institution edge. Succeed and choose: leave them in place as a turned channel, parade them before the world for scandal and infamy, or lock them in a quiet cell. Fail and they bolt - though the blown network burns either way.
[*][b]NEW: Prisoners and ransoms.[/b] A captured operative sits in foreign cells for up to five years, each year risking that they talk while the captor profits. Ransom them home with the new Operative Repatriation treaty article, disavow them, or trust their silence - masters never break.
[*][b]NEW: Naval Intelligence Network[/b] - infiltrate an admiralty through a journal-entry operation balancing Infiltration against Exposure, then choose your coup: crack their codes, cripple their flagship (The Great Wave), or copy their coastal surveys.
[*][b]NEW: Election interference[/b] - pick any party on the target's ballot from a console section and flood its campaign with momentum every month, invisibly. One choice per campaign, then results on your desk: exposure craters their electoral confidence and closes the channel, victory seats a well-disposed government that resists your leverage poorly.
[*][b]NEW: The Sealed Train[/b] - choose which exiled revolutionary rides into a rival power, by portrait, ideology and interest group, and hear whether the spark catches or the border police were waiting.
[*][b]NEW: Clandestine Arms Pipeline[/b] - fund and arm a belligerent without joining their war: delivery reports, a blockade-running interception gauntlet, an ultimatum when the enemy finally names you.
[*][b]NEW: Turned Networks, False Flags and Kompromat[/b] - victims with superior espionage can turn a network and feed its master nothing or poisoned technology; frame a patsy for your detected operations (now visible in the console, with real upkeep and an early cancel); compile yearly dossiers on enemy commanders - disgrace, ruin, publish, or file away unused.
[*][b]NEW: Blackmailed Concession[/b] - a dossier-backed treaty article that compels cooperation while your network stands; it collapses if the spies are rolled up.
[*][b]NEW: Fund Black Market Slavery[/b] - bankroll contraband slave routes through a target country into your own markets. Requires your own slavery laws; can be disabled via game rule.
[*][b]Steal Commander, Sabotage Recruitment and Develop Nation completed[/b] - true commander defection via character transfer, conscription sabotage with full events, and patient modernisation of a minor power that owes you everything.
[*][b]NEW: Three new External Security laws.[/b] Consular Intelligence, the Directorate of State Security, and Deniable Assets - five laws in all, and the espionage institution lists which operations each investment level unlocks.
[*][b]NEW: The Shadow War[/b] - a global intelligence scoreboard; every operation scores, scores decay, and the leading service holds Master of the Shadow War.
[*][b]NEW: Dynamic odds[/b] - institution edge, tradecraft match and operative experience all drive monthly success chances, capped at three in four.
[*]Operation upkeep genuinely scales with the target's economy - richer targets cost proportionally more, and a serious espionage program is a real budget line.
[*]Fixed a bug as old as the mod: operations against several countries at once could resolve against the wrong target.
[*]Fund Piracy, Sabotage Industry and Steal Ship Designs removed (superseded by 1.13 mechanics and the new systems). Full French localisation for everything.
[*][b]This release is not save-compatible with 3.x.[/b] Please start a new campaign.
[/list]

